\fs24 \cf2 IMPORTANT POWER NOTICE:
\f3\b0  The RF-NANO and Relay modules are powered by the 5V Isolated AC-DC supply. However, the 
\f4\b PWM to 0-10V Module
\f3\b0  typically requires an external 12V-24V power source (usually sourced directly from the welder's internal mainboard) to successfully generate a 10V output.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sl276\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f4\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Main Power:
\f3\b0  Connect the 5V Isolated supply to the 
\f4\b 5V
\f3\b0  and 
\f4\b GND
\f3\b0  pins of the RF-NANO.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Filter:
\f3\b0  Solder the 
\f4\b 100\'b5F
\f3\b0  capacitor between 
\f4\b 5V and GND
\f3\b0 .\uc0\u8232 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
PWM Signal (Amperage):
\f3\b0  Pin 
\f4\b D3
\f3\b0  connects to the PWM input of the 0-10V converter module.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Relay 1 (Torch Trigger):
\f3\b0  Pin 
\f4\b D4
\f3\b0  controls this relay. The relay's Common (COM) and Normally Open (NO) pins connect to the welder's trigger wires.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Relay 2 (GND Isolation):
\f3\b0  Pin 
\f4\b D5
\f3\b0  controls this relay. This relay physically disconnects the ground (GND) of the welder's amperage control when the pedal is at rest. This completely eliminates low-end electrical noise.\uc0\u8232 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sl276\partightenfactor0
