\fs24 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Thermal & Electrical Isolation:
\f3\b0  The receiver must be installed in a non-conductive enclosure to protect it from metal dust, heat, and direct high-frequency arcs inside the welding machine.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls6\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Relay Advantage:
\f3\b0  The use of mechanical 
\f4\b HJR-4102-L-5V
\f3\b0  relays ensures absolute zero leakage current when the pedal is not pressed. Relay 2 strictly disconnects the potentiometer ground, completely neutralizing any phantom voltages or electrical noise that could confuse the welder's logic board at 0% throttle.\uc0\u8232 \
\ls6\ilvl0
\f4\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3.	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Fail Safe System:
\f3\b0  If the pedal runs out of battery, goes out of range, or suffers from severe electromagnetic interference, the receiver will automatically trigger the 
\f5\i Fail Safe
\f3\i0  protocol in under 0.8 seconds, shutting down the relays and stopping the welding arc immediately.\uc0\u8232 \
}